<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBQA-F001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBQA-F001" ;
  triage:title "Dead, wrongly-mapped test-only constructor PyNudge::from_post_send" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-graft-python/src/lib.rs:245 -- PyNudge::from_post_send was newly introduced by sprint AZ.1 (commit 5249a8558), is not a #[pymethods] function, is not registered on _atm_graft, and has exactly one caller in the whole workspace: the unit test at line 1296. It also encodes the wrong contract (body = event.title.clone()) versus the real production path from_host_nudge, where body must be the canonical rendered <atm ...> text and notice_text the title-only display string. Confirmed via grep against the pinned commit -- exactly 2 occurrences (definition + one test call). Fix: delete from_post_send and rewrite its one test against the real from_host_nudge path, or delete the test if it adds no coverage." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "dead-code-wrong-contract" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-10T17:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
